{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1410088-identifying-nephandi-and-widderslainte","id":1410088,"title":"Identifying Nephandi and Widderslainte","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-24T09:47:21-07:00","id":1410088,"title":"Identifying Nephandi and Widderslainte","content":"Hi. <br /> <br /> Is it possible to identify Nephandi or Widderslainte by &quot;testing&quot; their corrupt Avatars somehow? How else can you identify them? Do their magic leave a &quot;trace&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T11:08:18-07:00","id":1410100,"title":"","content":"The books are kind of hazy on this. Theoretically it should be possible, but practically it is likely so difficult as to be impossible. <br /> <br /> The first big indication of this is that the Nephandi are said to be able to infiltrate almost anyone. If it were easy to test for them this wouldn't be likely.<br /> <br /> The second is the Amanda storyline spread out over the 2nd edition books. One of Senex' students went Nephandi. He killed her and <i>maybe</i> fixed her Avatar. Her reincarnation is under constant suspicion of being a Widderslainte. Senex might be sure if he succeeded or not but no one else is, so if there is a way of detection it is not something most people have access to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T13:24:02-07:00","id":1410122,"title":"","content":"The Sidhe of House Ailil can sense a Nependi in a 100 yards perimeter<br /> <br /> With a 8 perception roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T13:35:59-07:00","id":1410125,"title":"","content":"See M20 Book of the Fallen, pages 151-152, for 'Shroud the Soul' that Nephandi use to hide their aura (Prime 4 also hides Resonance). As it's only a Mind 1 Prime 2 effect (Prime 4 hides Resonance), that's a pretty basic way not to see a Nephandi. Also, any Arcane makes it harder to find out their true nature.<br /> <br /> Magic can leave traces but you can't always trace the magic to a specific individual. So, if a Nephandi cast a dark Life effect, it might be noted. The characters noting it would still have to track them down.<br /> <br /> Avatars require Mind 3 and Prime 2 and Spirit 1 to see in Mage 20. If you have the Nephandus able to cloud their Avatar, it's harder to see. There's an 'Innocuous Aura' Merit and a 'Qlippotich Radiance' Flaw if you go into those realms to make Nephandi easier or harder to find.<br /> <br /> Any Nephandi with long-term plans is going to have to hide their aura and Avatar. The more Resonance they have, the harder they'll have to work to confuse those with detection capabilities. Sleepers don't see auras, so that means it's up to mages or other supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T15:29:08-07:00","id":1410142,"title":"","content":"Cool, I get it.<br /> <br /> The particular case I have in my chronicle is: a Widderslainte is about to be sentenced for crimes against sleepers. Shes the reincarnation of a notorious Nephandus and her being a Widderslainte will be important to establish the sentence. Clarifying even further: this current incarnation hasnt gone through the cauls (or whatever process akin to &quot;dancing the Spiral&quot; Nephandi may have).<br /> <br /> Is it possible to have access to the Avatars previous lifes (maybe with Time And Spirit?) to confirm it used to belong to the aforementioned Nephandus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T16:45:19-07:00","id":1410152,"title":"","content":"The Akashic Brotherhood and Euthanatos both have factions which track Avatars and keep records of them. So, they could try and find a past incarnation of one of their members. Other groups don't seem to have the same tracking in canon, but if the notorious Nephandi's Avatar was known, then it's possible someone kept a record.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T18:20:34-07:00","id":1410173,"title":"","content":"I had forgotten about the Euthanatos/Akashics doing that. Actually, I dont see why you couldnt use a Rote combining Spirit and Time to do it.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T07:23:52-07:00","id":1410285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1410088-identifying-nephandi-and-widderslainte?p=1410142#post1410142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool, I get it.<br /> <br /> The particular case I have in my chronicle is: a Widderslainte is about to be sentenced for crimes against sleepers. Shes the reincarnation of a notorious Nephandus and her being a Widderslainte will be important to establish the sentence. Clarifying even further: this current incarnation hasnt gone through the cauls (or whatever process akin to &quot;dancing the Spiral&quot; Nephandi may have).<br /> <br /> Is it possible to have access to the Avatars previous lifes (maybe with Time And Spirit?) to confirm it used to belong to the aforementioned Nephandus?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Widderslainte don't need to go through the Cauls, their Avatars are already inverted. Usually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T08:26:35-07:00","id":1410301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1410088-identifying-nephandi-and-widderslainte#post1410088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi.<br /> <br /> Is it possible to identify Nephandi or Widderslainte by &quot;testing&quot; their corrupt Avatars somehow? How else can you identify them? Do their magic leave a &quot;trace&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>There a story about a Batini Mage - Miriam Ben-Hamida - who clearly saw that her husband was a Nephandus (and decided to kill him and to attempt to purify his Avatar) . It is implied that due to her being an Adept (level 4) of Spirit she was able to sense the change in her husband.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 08-25-2020, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T09:14:04-07:00","id":1410310,"title":"","content":"What you're looking for are the rules on Resonance: Nephandi tend to accumulate Resonance that's tainted by their Magick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T19:15:51-07:00","id":1411145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1410088-identifying-nephandi-and-widderslainte?p=1410285#post1410285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Widderslainte don't need to go through the Cauls, their Avatars are already inverted. Usually.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, canonically, all widderslainte are destined to be &quot;evil&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T19:33:55-07:00","id":1411148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1410088-identifying-nephandi-and-widderslainte?p=1411145#post1411145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So, canonically, all widderslainte are destined to be &quot;evil&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 Book of the Fallen, especially if you listen to the developers Phil Brucato and Jacqueline Byrk on the Mage: the Podcast episode about it, gives you a small chance for widderslainte to be non-evil. The Avatar of a widderslainte is going to push the person it is in towards being a Nephandus, but those characters do not have to do as their Avatar wants.<br /> <br /> In canon, you basically only have Amanda as redeemed and by an Arch-Mage, so many mages are likely to believe widderslainte are inherently evil.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T19:43:43-07:00","id":1411151,"title":"","content":"That is actually one of the topics I want to bring into my chronicle. In my headcanon, widderslainte are not &quot;evil&quot; per se, but they do have their avatar pushing them to do &quot;evil&quot; when they have the chance. Then, the mage community will be divided about what to do with them, as some will think they deserve a chance and some will want to root them out at first sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T05:47:21-07:00","id":1411200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1410088-identifying-nephandi-and-widderslainte?p=1411151#post1411151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is actually one of the topics I want to bring into my chronicle. In my headcanon, widderslainte are not &quot;evil&quot; per se, but they do have their avatar pushing them to do &quot;evil&quot; when they have the chance. Then, the mage community will be divided about what to do with them, as some will think they deserve a chance and some will want to root them out at first sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just pushing them to do evil. Avatars have a lot of ability to manipulate a mage's senses and perceptions. Resisting a Nephandic Avatar is not just about the will to reject its urges but also about the wisdom to see through its manipulations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T06:16:15-07:00","id":1411204,"title":"","content":"Much more interesting, then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}